#
# Conformance case: foundation/identity-overlap-mixiden
# AC: foundation lowering — OntoUML MixIden discipline (issue #503).
#
# Reproduces reasoning_lint.identity_overlap: every endurant instantiates exactly
# one Kind, so no logic:Kind may specialize another logic:Kind. ex:Dog is a
# logic:Kind that specializes the logic:Kind ex:Animal → logic:MixIden. ex:Animal
# is a clean top logic:Kind (no Kind ancestor) and trips nothing — the negative
# control.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema facts
# (the two Kind puns + the logic:subClassOf edge) are duplicated there in the
# named world ex:schema; these declarations are the program axioms the projections
# need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/identity-overlap-mixiden/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: two Kinds + a Kind-⊑-Kind edge (also asserted as world facts in input.nq).
ex:Dog    a logic:Kind .
ex:Animal a logic:Kind .
ex:Dog    logic:subClassOf ex:Animal .
